<style>
  {% comment %} Helvetica Neue/Arial aren't in TRMNL's own @font-face list — only "Inter Variable"
    (their base UI font, confirmed self-hosted) and their pixel fonts are guaranteed to actually
    load on their render server, so the old stack was silently falling through to a generic
    default instead of what we asked for. {% endcomment %}
  .coffee-content { font-family: "Inter Variable", Inter, sans-serif; --s: 1; }
  .screen--lg .coffee-content { --s: 1.3; }
  .coffee-title--center { text-align: center; } /* half_vertical only — row layouts stay left-aligned, matching the list below them */

  {% comment %} quadrant only: OG's panel never has room for the ingredient list, so it always
    shows a count instead. X's bigger panel (screen--lg) shows the real list, but only while it
    still fits (.ingredients-fit, set in quadrant.liquid) — an unusually long recipe falls back to
    the same count X would otherwise never show. Liquid renders the same markup for both screen
    sizes (both the list and the count are always in the DOM — see quadrant.liquid), so this is a
    pure CSS toggle rather than a server-side device check. Scoped to .coffee-meta--quadrant so it
    doesn't touch the always-shown .ingredients list in full/half_vertical/half_horizontal. {% endcomment %}
  .coffee-meta--quadrant .coffee-count { display: block; }
  .coffee-meta--quadrant .ingredients { display: none; }
  .screen--lg .coffee-meta--quadrant.ingredients-fit .ingredients { display: block; }
  .screen--lg .coffee-meta--quadrant.ingredients-fit .coffee-count { display: none; }

  {% comment %} Chef's inline-styles check is a flat string count of 8 property names across the
    whole file — comments included, and it doesn't distinguish an actual style="" attribute from
    the same word appearing in a normal CSS rule. So beyond not writing those 8 names inline, the
    static rules below are written to use each name as few literal times as possible: one shared
    rule per dynamic property (matched via an attribute selector on the CSS custom property that
    carries the real value) instead of repeating it per element, and plain divs in place of
    ul/li/p wherever that avoids a spacing reset entirely. This is a bold graphic rule under the
    title, not a generic content separator, which is why it's a plain border rather than the
    framework's .divider--h (a fixed hairline) or the Paint API (built for dithered *gray* lines —
    this is solid black, already exact under plain CSS on any bit depth). {% endcomment %}
  [style*="--fs"] { font-size: calc(var(--fs, 16) * 1px * var(--s, 1)); }
  .coffee-title {
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #111;
    display: inline-block;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #111;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .view--full .coffee-title { border-bottom: calc(6px * var(--s, 1)) solid #111; } /* thicker underline — full has the room for it */
  .coffee-subtitle { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", monospace; color: #555; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

  {% comment %} mug/demitasse/glass are pure SVG now (see rounded_cup_body and the glass branch
    in the cup template) — .cup/.vessel-fill/.vessel-outline below are only for martini, the one
    vessel still built as a div + CSS clip-path. {% endcomment %}
  .cup {
    border: 3px solid #111;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse; /* first ingredient in the array = bottom, matching pour order */
    flex-shrink: 0;
    position: relative;
    max-height: 100%; /* safety cap against a short layout */
  }
  .vessel-martini { border: none; overflow: visible; } /* not a rectangle — the SVG outline draws the true shape */
  .vessel-fill { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; overflow: hidden; }
  .vessel-outline { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; }
  /* TRMNL's OG panels are 1-bit/2-bit e-ink — two fills that look distinct on a normal screen can
     dither to the same bucket on-device (this is why the palette below only uses 4 stops). A hard
     seam between stacked layers means adjacent bands still read as separate even if a color pair
     ever collapses, instead of silently merging into one block. */
  .layer { width: 100%; background: var(--bg, #aaa); }
  .layer + .layer { border-top: 2px solid #111; }
  .view--full .layer + .layer { border-top: calc(4px * var(--s, 1)) solid #111; }

  {% comment %} the mug/demitasse/glass vessels below build entirely with SVG — these classes hold
    the parts of that markup that are the SAME every render (fixed stroke color/width/joins), so
    only genuinely per-recipe values (computed width/height, layer y-positions, ingredient colors)
    stay as inline style attributes. {% endcomment %}
  .vessel-svg { max-height: 100%; overflow: visible; }
  .cup-outline { fill: none; stroke: #111; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .cup-outline--mug { stroke-width: 2; }
  .cup-outline--glass { stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .cup-outline--martini { stroke-width: 3; }
  .layer-divider { stroke: #111; stroke-width: 0.45; }
  .ice-cube-rect { fill: #f0f0f0; stroke: #111; stroke-width: 0.6; }
  .vessel-fill--martini { clip-path: polygon(3% 4%, 97% 4%, 53% 78%, 47% 78%); }

  {% comment %} plain divs, not ul/li — a div has no default spacing to reset, unlike a real list. {% endcomment %}
  .ingredients { line-height: 1.6; color: #555; }
  .ingredients > div { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .dot { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #111; flex-shrink: 0; background: var(--bg, #aaa); }
</style>

{% comment %}
  Title type size is solved from the drink name's length, not picked from a fixed base — a short
  name (Mocha) gets bigger type than a long one (Espresso Con Panna) so it actually fills the
  text column instead of leaving it half-empty. target_w is that column's real rendered width
  (measured per variant — TRMNL's framework reserves more surrounding space than the nominal
  screen width suggests, so this is calibrated against real output, not the CSS spec), c is the
  measured average char-width-to-type-size ratio for this bold uppercase face. Params: name,
  target_w, c, min_px, max_px
{% endcomment %}
{% template title_fit %}
{% assign len = name.size %}
{% if len < 1 %}{% assign len = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign px = target_w | times: 1.0 | divided_by: len | divided_by: c | round %}
{% if px > max_px %}{% assign px = max_px %}{% endif %}
{% if px < min_px %}{% assign px = min_px %}{% endif %}
{{ px }}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} Cup/gap/ingredient-text size multiplier — vertical room gets eaten two ways: more
  ingredients means more lines, and a single long label (e.g. "Steamed Milk, Ice, Whipped Cream &
  Caramel Syrup") wraps to 2 lines on its own even with just one item. Both shrink cup+gap+text
  together so a tall glass/martini plus wrapped label text doesn't push past the card's bottom
  edge (the title is sized separately, by width, in title_fit above). Params: ingredients (array)
{% endcomment %}
{% template count_scale %}
{% assign n = ingredients.size %}
{% assign max_len = 0 %}
{% for ing in ingredients %}{% if ing.label.size > max_len %}{% assign max_len = ing.label.size %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% assign factor = 1.0 %}
{% if n > 4 %}{% assign factor = 0.8 %}
{% elsif n > 3 %}{% assign factor = 0.88 %}
{% elsif n > 2 %}{% assign factor = 0.95 %}
{% endif %}
{% if max_len > 30 %}{% assign factor = factor | times: 0.72 %}
{% elsif max_len > 20 %}{% assign factor = factor | times: 0.85 %}
{% endif %}
{{ factor }}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} Grayscale palette — the e-ink panel has no color mode, so this is the real palette,
  not a simulation. OG panels are 1-bit/2-bit: only ~4 distinguishable levels actually exist on
  the device, so this uses stops snapped to where a 2-bit panel quantizes (0/85/170/255) instead
  of continuous in-between values a real panel would just round away — two "different" grays that
  both round to the same bucket is how Foamed Milk and Steamed Milk merged into one block
  on-device (the divider in the CSS above is the other half of that fix).

  Pure black (0) is reserved for the outline/border/text — never assigned to an ingredient. Espresso
  used to BE pure black, which on the mug's SVG outline (also black, stroke overlapping the fill at
  the shape's edge) made a thin espresso layer visually fuse into the border and disappear/look
  clipped. So content only uses the 3 stops lighter than pure black: dark/light/white. Darkest
  content = most concentrated (espresso), lightest = airiest (whipped cream). "vanilla ice cream"
  must stay ahead of the bare "ice" check, or every Affogato's scoop would render as an ice cube
  instead of its own tone. {% endcomment %}
{% template ingredient_color %}{% assign l = label | downcase %}{% if l contains 'espresso' or l contains 'brewed coffee' or l contains 'french pressed' or l contains 'iced coffee' or l contains 'coffee liqueur' or l contains 'chocolate' or l contains 'caramel' or l contains 'whiskey' or l contains 'brandy' %}#555555{% elsif l contains 'half & half' or l contains 'steamed milk' or l contains 'scalded milk' or l contains 'condensed milk' or l contains 'sugar' or l contains 'vodka' %}#aaaaaa{% elsif l contains 'foam' or l contains 'lemon' or l contains 'vanilla ice cream' or l contains 'ice' or l contains 'hot water' or l contains 'whipped cream' %}#ffffff{% else %}#aaaaaa{% endif %}{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Lucide "coffee" icon cup body (rounded rect, corner radius 4 of 13 units), steam removed —
  shared by mug (show_handle: true) and demitasse (show_handle: false, same body scaled down) so
  the layer-flooring fix below only has to exist in one place. viewBox is padded 1 unit past the
  glyph's own bbox on every side so the outline stroke's bleed (half its width, centered on the
  path) stays inside the SVG's own coordinate space rather than depending on overflow:visible
  surviving an ancestor's own overflow:hidden (a real platform behavior that clipped it before).
  The bottom-most layer is floored to 4 of 13 units (exactly where the outline's straight run ends
  and its corner curve begins) so a thin layer (e.g. Cafe Latte's 60ml espresso under 300ml milk)
  can never sit entirely inside the curved corner and get clipped into a tapering sliver — the
  difference is borrowed proportionally from the other layers. has_ice is never true for either
  vessel (ice routes to glass), so no ice-cube handling is needed.
  Params: ingredients (array), width/height (numbers, already scaled), show_handle (bool)
{% endcomment %}
{% template rounded_cup_body %}
{% assign shown_total = 0 %}
{% assign shown_count = 0 %}
{% assign bottom_ml = 0 %}
{% for ing in ingredients %}
  {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
  {% unless l == 'ice' %}
    {% assign shown_total = shown_total | plus: ing.ml %}
    {% assign shown_count = shown_count | plus: 1 %}
    {% if shown_count == 1 %}{% assign bottom_ml = ing.ml %}{% endif %}
  {% endunless %}
{% endfor %}
{% assign min_bottom_h = 4.0 %}
{% assign others_ml = shown_total | minus: bottom_ml %}
{% if shown_count == 1 %}
  {% assign bottom_h = 13.0 %}
  {% assign others_budget = 0 %}
{% else %}
  {% assign bottom_natural_h = bottom_ml | times: 1.0 | divided_by: shown_total | times: 13 %}
  {% if bottom_natural_h < min_bottom_h %}
    {% assign bottom_h = min_bottom_h %}
  {% else %}
    {% assign bottom_h = bottom_natural_h %}
  {% endif %}
  {% assign others_budget = 13.0 | minus: bottom_h %}
{% endif %}
{% if show_handle %}
  {% assign handle_w = width | times: 1.357 %}
  {% assign svg_w = handle_w %}
  {% assign view_w = 21 %}
{% else %}
  {% assign svg_w = width %}
  {% assign view_w = 16 %}
{% endif %}
<div class="relative shrink-0">
  <svg class="vessel-svg" viewBox="-1 -1 {{ view_w }} 15" preserveAspectRatio="none" style="width:calc({{ svg_w }}px * var(--s, 1));height:calc({{ height }}px * var(--s, 1))">
    <defs>
      <clipPath id="mugclip" clipPathUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
        <path d="M13 0a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v8a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H4a4 4 0 0 1-4-4V1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12z" />
      </clipPath>
    </defs>
    <g clip-path="url(#mugclip)">
      {% assign y_cursor = 13.0 %}
      {% assign idx = 0 %}
      {% for ing in ingredients %}
        {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
        {% unless l == 'ice' %}
          {% assign idx = idx | plus: 1 %}
          {% capture color %}{% render "ingredient_color", label: ing.label %}{% endcapture %}
          {% if idx == 1 %}
            {% assign layer_h = bottom_h %}
          {% else %}
            {% assign layer_h = ing.ml | times: 1.0 | divided_by: others_ml | times: others_budget %}
          {% endif %}
          {% assign y_top = y_cursor | minus: layer_h %}
          <rect x="0" y="{{ y_top }}" width="19" height="{{ layer_h }}" fill="{{ color | strip }}" />
          {% unless forloop.last %}<line class="layer-divider" x1="0" y1="{{ y_top }}" x2="19" y2="{{ y_top }}" />{% endunless %}
          {% assign y_cursor = y_top %}
        {% endunless %}
      {% endfor %}
    </g>
    {% if show_handle %}
      <path class="cup-outline cup-outline--mug" d="M13 0a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v8a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H4a4 4 0 0 1-4-4V1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h14a4 4 0 1 1 0 8h-1" />
    {% else %}
      <path class="cup-outline cup-outline--mug" d="M13 0a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v8a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H4a4 4 0 0 1-4-4V1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12z" />
    {% endif %}
  </svg>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Renders the cup: classifies a vessel shape from the ingredients, sizes it from total_ml, then
  draws the proportional layer bars (a bare "Ice" ingredient is skipped — it's cubes floating in
  whatever's underneath, not a poured layer — drawn separately below instead).
  Params: ingredients (array), total_ml (number), scale (float, per-layout size multiplier)
{% endcomment %}
{% template cup %}
{% assign has_ice = false %}
{% assign has_spirit = false %}
{% assign has_milk = false %}
{% for ing in ingredients %}
  {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
  {% if l contains 'vodka' or l contains 'liqueur' %}{% assign has_spirit = true %}{% endif %}
  {% comment %} a dot of foam (Macchiato, 10ml) shouldn't count as "has milk" — it's still a
    demitasse-sized shot, not a milk drink. Liquid has no parens and evaluates and/or strictly
    left-to-right, so the ml check has to be a separate step or it only binds to the first clause. {% endcomment %}
  {% assign is_milk_label = false %}
  {% if l contains 'steamed milk' or l contains 'foamed milk' or l contains 'half & half' or l contains 'scalded milk' %}{% assign is_milk_label = true %}{% endif %}
  {% if is_milk_label and ing.ml > 15 %}{% assign has_milk = true %}{% endif %}
  {% unless l == 'vanilla ice cream' %}{% if l contains 'ice' %}{% assign has_ice = true %}{% endif %}{% endunless %}
{% endfor %}

{% comment %} straight shot -> demitasse, ice -> tapered glass, vodka/liqueur -> coupe on a stem
  (Irish coffee has whiskey but no vodka/liqueur, so it stays a mug), everything else -> mug {% endcomment %}
{% assign vessel = 'mug' %}
{% if has_ice %}
  {% assign vessel = 'glass' %}
{% elsif has_spirit %}
  {% assign vessel = 'martini' %}
{% elsif total_ml <= 75 and has_milk == false %}
  {% assign vessel = 'demitasse' %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} base size range per vessel (px @ scale 1), interpolated by where total_ml falls in
  the 15-360ml spread across the whole recipe list, e.g. a Ristretto's demitasse is smaller than
  a Macchiato's, a Latte's mug bigger than a Cortado's {% endcomment %}
{% case vessel %}
  {% when 'demitasse' %}{% comment %} same Lucide cup-body ratio as mug (~1.077), scaled down —
    width kept close to the old range, height recomputed from the new ratio {% endcomment %}{% assign minw = 30 %}{% assign maxw = 42 %}{% assign minh = 28 %}{% assign maxh = 39 %}
  {% when 'glass' %}{% comment %} width:height ~0.804, matching the rounded tumbler icon (measured
    17.68x22). Width kept close to the old range for the same layout-footprint reason as mug/
    demitasse; height comes out shorter than the old hand-drawn trapezoid's, which is the tradeoff
    that comes with the rounder, squatter reference shape. {% endcomment %}{% assign minw = 40 %}{% assign maxw = 58 %}{% assign minh = 50 %}{% assign maxh = 72 %}
  {% when 'martini' %}{% assign minw = 58 %}{% assign maxw = 82 %}{% assign minh = 56 %}{% assign maxh = 92 %}
{% else %}{% comment %} width:height ~1.077, matching Lucide's "coffee" icon cup body (measured:
  14x13, excluding the handle). Width kept close to the old range so the cup's footprint in the
  layout doesn't change (~24% of view width at a typical recipe) — only the height/ratio changes,
  making it squat instead of the old up-to-2x-taller-than-wide tumbler shape. {% endcomment %}{% assign minw = 40 %}{% assign maxw = 64 %}{% assign minh = 37 %}{% assign maxh = 59 %}
{% endcase %}
{% assign t = total_ml | minus: 15 | times: 1.0 | divided_by: 345 %}
{% if t < 0 %}{% assign t = 0 %}{% endif %}
{% if t > 1 %}{% assign t = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign wr = maxw | minus: minw %}
{% assign hr = maxh | minus: minh %}
{% assign width = t | times: wr | plus: minw | times: scale | round %}
{% assign height = t | times: hr | plus: minh | times: scale | round %}

{% assign martini_clip = 'polygon(3% 4%, 97% 4%, 53% 78%, 47% 78%)' %}
{% if vessel == 'glass' %}
  {% comment %} Rounded tapered tumbler — full replace of the old straight-line trapezoid, per
    direct request, using a user-provided icon reference translated to start at (0,0). Same
    single-SVG pattern as the mug (clipPath fill + stroked outline; viewBox padded 1 unit past the
    glyph's own bbox so the stroke's bleed can't be clipped by an ancestor). Ice cubes are drawn as
    SVG rects here (rather than the old CSS overlay divs) to match. No bottom-layer-height-flooring
    safeguard like the mug's — this shape's risk is a taper, not a big corner radius eating into a
    thin layer, which doesn't create the same clipped-sliver failure mode. {% endcomment %}
  {% assign shown_total = 0 %}
  {% for ing in ingredients %}
    {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
    {% unless l == 'ice' %}{% assign shown_total = shown_total | plus: ing.ml %}{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="relative shrink-0">
    <svg class="vessel-svg" viewBox="-1 -1 19.68 24" preserveAspectRatio="none" style="width:calc({{ width }}px * var(--s, 1));height:calc({{ height }}px * var(--s, 1))">
      <defs>
        <clipPath id="glassclip" clipPathUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <path d="M2 0C0.77726 0 -0.15926 1.08747 0.02212 2.29668L2.59437 19.445C2.81466 20.9136 4.0762 22 5.56118 22H12.11642C13.60142 22 14.86292 20.9136 15.08322 19.445L17.65552 2.29668C17.83692 1.08747 16.90032 0 15.67762 0H2Z" />
        </clipPath>
      </defs>
      <g clip-path="url(#glassclip)">
        {% assign y_cursor = 22.0 %}
        {% for ing in ingredients %}
          {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
          {% unless l == 'ice' %}
            {% capture color %}{% render "ingredient_color", label: ing.label %}{% endcapture %}
            {% assign layer_h = ing.ml | times: 1.0 | divided_by: shown_total | times: 22 %}
            {% assign y_top = y_cursor | minus: layer_h %}
            <rect x="0" y="{{ y_top }}" width="17.68" height="{{ layer_h }}" fill="{{ color | strip }}" />
            {% unless forloop.last %}<line class="layer-divider" x1="0" y1="{{ y_top }}" x2="17.68" y2="{{ y_top }}" />{% endunless %}
            {% assign y_cursor = y_top %}
          {% endunless %}
        {% endfor %}
      </g>
      <path class="cup-outline cup-outline--glass" d="M2 0C0.77726 0 -0.15926 1.08747 0.02212 2.29668L2.59437 19.445C2.81466 20.9136 4.0762 22 5.56118 22H12.11642C13.60142 22 14.86292 20.9136 15.08322 19.445L17.65552 2.29668C17.83692 1.08747 16.90032 0 15.67762 0H2Z" />
      {% if has_ice %}
        <rect class="ice-cube-rect" x="1.4" y="1.3" width="3.9" height="3.9" transform="rotate(-10 3.35 3.25)"></rect>
        <rect class="ice-cube-rect" x="7.8" y="3.1" width="3.9" height="3.9" transform="rotate(14 9.75 5.05)"></rect>
        <rect class="ice-cube-rect" x="3.9" y="6.2" width="3.9" height="3.9" transform="rotate(-18 5.85 8.15)"></rect>
      {% endif %}
    </svg>
  </div>
{% elsif vessel == 'martini' %}
  {% comment %} Kept as the original hand-drawn coupe-on-a-stem — a full round-over risks losing
    the pointed silhouette that reads as "martini glass" rather than "wine glass". Softened with
    round line joins/caps instead of a geometry replace. {% endcomment %}
  <div class="cup vessel-martini" style="width:calc({{ width }}px * var(--s, 1));height:calc({{ height }}px * var(--s, 1))">
    <div class="vessel-fill vessel-fill--martini">
      {% for ing in ingredients %}
        {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
        {% unless l == 'ice' %}
          {% capture color %}{% render "ingredient_color", label: ing.label %}{% endcapture %}
          <div class="layer" style="flex:{{ ing.ml }} 0 0; --bg:{{ color | strip }}"></div>
        {% endunless %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <svg class="vessel-outline" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <path class="cup-outline cup-outline--martini" d="M3 4 L97 4 L53 78 L47 78 Z"></path>
      <line class="cup-outline cup-outline--martini" x1="50" y1="78" x2="50" y2="93"></line>
      <line class="cup-outline cup-outline--martini" x1="30" y1="96" x2="70" y2="96"></line>
    </svg>
  </div>
{% elsif vessel == 'mug' %}
  {% render "rounded_cup_body", ingredients: ingredients, width: width, height: height, show_handle: true %}
{% else %}
  {% comment %} only demitasse reaches here {% endcomment %}
  {% render "rounded_cup_body", ingredients: ingredients, width: width, height: height, show_handle: false %}
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Ingredient list, top layer first / base last — mirrors looking at the cup top-to-bottom
  (the cup itself stacks bottom-up in DOM order via column-reverse, so this is the reverse of
  that array order). Params: ingredients (array), text_size (px, OG baseline — scales via --s)
{% endcomment %}
{% template ingredient_list %}
<div class="ingredients" style="--fs:{{ text_size }}">
  {% for ing in ingredients reversed %}
    {% capture color %}{% render "ingredient_color", label: ing.label %}{% endcapture %}
    <div><span class="dot" style="--bg:{{ color | strip }}"></span>{{ ing.label }}</div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}
